appendix.Functional Requirements:
Information Sharing by Personnel:
When sharing Information, the person who handles the information is responsible to ensure that the receiver is authorized to see the relevant information, as well as to check if there are sufficient grounds (business justification) for sharing it. In case Information is asked to be shared by the Information receiver, the information receiver is responsible for providing a sufficient business justification for receiving specific Information. 
When sharing Information, the Employee who handles the Information is responsible for ensuring that the receiver knows the information classification (AC-16) of the relevant Information, so that the Information receiver knows which secure handling requirements and protection controls apply:
an internal receiver (the Employee) by default should know the information classification 
An external receiver can be notified about information classification classes by adding a disclaimer with an explanation about the Information criticality and expected protection controls.
If a person gets the Information (e.g., documents, emails, etc.) that was not meant to be received and/or seen by them or does not belong to them in any way, the receiver must return it to the sender and delete it. The sender must inform their manager and report an incident. 
It is not allowed to have verbal conversations about sensitive Luminor Information in public places or places where unauthorized persons could hear.
It is only allowed to use communication channels that are controlled by Luminor for sharing Luminor Information.
Controls for Personnel information sharing:
When sending Information externally:
Make sure that it is necessary for performance of business functions as described and approved in Luminor internal regulations regulating a specific Information flow to an external recipient;
Use strong cryptography algorithms for Information encryption (e.g. AES256 algorithm for encrypting with ZIP archive);
Use approved methods for sending Information;
Decryption key (e.g. password) must be shared using another communication channel.
It is prohibited to place sensitive Information in external websites (e.g. for translation into other languages).
When sending Information internally Class4 (strictly confidential):
Use strong cryptography algorithms for Information encryption (e.g. AES256 algorithm for encrypting with ZIP archive);
Use approved methods for sending Information;
Decryption key (e.g. password) must be shared using another communication channel.
Controls for IT systems for Information transfer:
Secure protocol usage for Information transfer; 
file encryption before information sending; 
Integration with Luminor PKI, secret manager, and other key management solutions;
Secure protocol usage with integrity protection capabilities for Information transfer (e.g. HTTPS, SSH).

