appendix.Functional Requirements:
Initial and Ongoing Training: 
Provide mandatory basic information security training to all new hires, within 30 days of joining the Luminor. 

Refresh the training content every 12 months or upon significant changes in information security framework, threat landscape or regulations and re-assign to personnel periodically. 


Basic information security training content:
Information security training must include at a minimum appropriate awareness of and competencies for:
classified information (including cardholder data) protection;
overview of information security risk types;
cybersecurity threat awareness within the financial services industry;
acceptable use of end-user technology, devices security;

safe online operating habits (for example, spam and Phishing, downloading files, browsing practices, Internet usage); 
unusual activity and IT security incidents reporting;
identification and authentication, password security, and protection:
how select and protect strong authentication factors;
instruction not to reuse previously used passwords/passphrase or how to change in case of any suspicion that it has been compromised;


AT-2(1): Practical Exercises or Testing Knowledge
Personnel knowledge of the content provided by Luminor in basic information security awareness training must be tested after completion and at least annually. 
If basic information security awareness training is organized by a service provider for its Employees, knowledge testing is recommended, but not mandatory. 

AT-2(3): Social Engineering and Mining (only for Employees):
Social engineering testing, including fake Phishing emails campaign, shall be performed at least annually to challenge and enhance Employees and information security awareness.

