appendix.Functional Requirements:
Protection of Luminor network perimeter boundaries [Central]:
Monitor and control communications at managed interfaces. 
SC-7(4): External Telecommunications Services. Implement a managed interface for each external telecommunication service:
Implement a managed interface for each external telecommunication service;
Establish a traffic flow policy for each managed interface;
Protect the confidentiality and integrity of the information being transmitted across each interface;
Document each exception to the traffic flow policy with a supporting mission or business need and duration of that need;
Review exceptions to the traffic flow policy on defined frequency and remove exceptions that are no longer supported by an explicit mission or business need;
Prevent unauthorized exchange of control plane traffic with external networks;
Publish information to enable remote networks to detect unauthorized control plane traffic from internal networks; and
Filter unauthorized control plane traffic from external networks.
Ensure the segregation and segmentation of systems and networks considering the criticality or importance of the function they support, the classification and the overall risk profile of assets using them;
Document and implement subnetworks for publicly accessible components, separating them from internal/trusted networks. All external incoming connection shall be terminated in DMZ. It is preferred to use separated DMZ for different web services or applications.
Use boundary protection devices (firewalls, security devices) to manage external connections or connections between two different network zones or segments. Follow Defence in depth principal – implement multiple layers of security enforcement points/controls and never allow direct connectivity to internal (trusted) Luminor networks from Untrusted Networks (e.g., Internet).
Use a separate and dedicated network for the administration of ICT assets;
Manage configuration changes of security devices/ firewall rules according to CM-3: Configuration Change Control.
Perform the review of firewall rules and connections filters on a regular basis. For the systems supporting critical or important functions, verify the adequacy of the existing firewall rules and connection filters at least every six months.
SC-7(3): Access Points. Limit the number of external network connections to the Luminor network and systems.
SC-7(5): Deny by Default – Allow by Exception. Deny network communications traffic by default and allow network communications traffic by exception.
SC-7(7): Split Tunneling for Remote Devices. Prevent split tunneling for remote devices unless securely provisioned.
SC-7(8): Route Traffic to Authenticated Proxy Servers. If needed, route internal communications traffic to external networks through authenticated proxy servers at managed interfaces.
SC-7(10): Prevent Exfiltration. Prevent information exfiltration through managed interfaces.
Ensure capability temporarily isolate, where necessary, subnetworks and network components and devices;
Protection of system (or dedicated area/value stream/domain) network boundaries [Local]:
	Monitor and control communications at the external managed interfaces to the system and at key internal managed interfaces within the system;
	Implement subnetworks for publicly accessible system components that are physically or logically separated from internal organizational networks; 
Connect to external networks or systems only through managed interfaces consisting of boundary protection devices arranged in accordance with an organizational security architecture.

